      "head_commit": {
        "id": "276be173312458722ffcb0876be8c9ae44a3f233",
        "tree_id": "b29347d7c7f6d9b85373e3efc0010c7ad91d43dd",
        "message": "fix(tests): make the system-health check pass without a live LLM backend\n\nThe LLM lane needs either a local Ollama on port 11434 or a configured cloud\nAPI key. A clean CI runner has neither, so LLMRouter.route() correctly returns\nNone — but the health check asserted a route was found, so it only ever passed\non a machine with a model running. That is the second cause of the CI failure.\n\nThe check now verifies the outcome that actually depends on the environment:\nwith a backend available the phrases must route, and without one they must\nnot. The tool catalogue check is machine-independent and always runs.\n\nCI also emits a workflow annotation naming each failing test, so a red run\nshows which test broke without needing to download the log artifact.\n\nVerified locally: 77/77 pass with no network, no voice profile, and no LLM\nbackend — the exact conditions of a GitHub-hosted runner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
